{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1451398-deviant-dumb-question-why-variations","id":1451398,"title":"[Deviant] Dumb question: why Variations?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Deviant: The Renegades"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-06-08T15:27:28-07:00","id":1451398,"title":"[Deviant] Dumb question: why Variations?","content":"I have bee reading Deviant: the Renegade and I since have a very simple and dumb question stuck in my head:<br /> <br /> <b>Shouldn't Variations be called Deviations, and vice versa?</b><br /> <br /> I mean, the game is called <i>Deviant</i>. The things that make the core power system of the game, the things that define what a Deviant is, that set how much they <i>deviate </i>from baseline humans... shouldn't be called <i>Deviations </i>instead of Variations?<br /> <br /> On the other hand, the things that add <i>variety </i>to that same power, and enable different <i>varieties </i>and, well, <i>variations</i>, on the same power... shouldn't be called <i>Variations </i>instead of Deviations?<br /> <br /> Keep in mind I am not a native English speaker, so perhaps there are some nuances I'm missing.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26440-moonwhisper","name":"moonwhisper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26440_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-08T16:48:15-07:00","id":1451405,"title":"","content":"As I understand it, the name of the gameline wasn't the original idea of the developers of the game, whose general naming inspiration came from early natural science terminology (Darwin being the most obvious example thereof). &quot;Variation&quot; is a pretty natural-sciency value-neutral way to describe different traits within a population, especially from the early period when genetics was itself still a field in formation. It also avoids identifying the Remade's &quot;positive&quot; abilities and properties as the &quot;primary&quot; means by which they &quot;deviate&quot; from baseline humanity; remember that Variations are contrasted with Scars, which make up at least as much of that difference, and sometimes much more. This isn't a problem for using &quot;Deviation&quot; to mean &quot;different manifestations of Variations and Scars,&quot; where the deviation in question is between those traits and not between the Remade and humanity.<br /> <br /> All that said, it's not a thought that hasn't crossed my mind now and then, either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}